...\nSouth Central Alamosa County in southeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 400 PM MST Wednesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding along the Conejos River, from Mogote downstream\nto Manassa, and the San Antonio River, near Ortiz downstream to\nManassa, is ongoing. Additional flooding of creeks, streams, and\nother low-lying and flood-prone locations is possible. Numerous\nroads remain closed due to flooding. Expect many areas of slow\nmoving or standing water through eastern Conejos County.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 347 PM MST, Upstream runoff from recent rain and snowmelt is\ncausing flooding into eastern Conejos County.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nManassa, Sanford, Antonito, Romeo, Alamosa East, Conejos and\nOrtiz.\n- http://www.water.noaa.gov","ends":"2026-11-04T16:00:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Alamosa, CO; Conejos, CO; Costilla, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b092e67b29472df648ea32d2432f2eb9c230c8e2.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b092e67b29472df648ea32d2432f2eb9c230c8e2.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued November 2 at 3:29PM MST until November 6 at 12:00AM MST by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"...The National Weather Service in Pueblo has issued a Flood Warning\nfor the following rivers in Colorado...\n\nRio Grande At Alamosa affecting Alamosa County.\n\n.Minor flooding along the Rio Grande through Alamosa is expected due\nto upstream flooding occurring in the vicinity of Monte Vista.\n\nFor the Rio Grande...including Alamosa...Minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...Rio Grande at Alamosa.\n\n* WHEN...From Wednesday afternoon to late Thursday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 9.0 feet, Minor flooding. Minor agricultural flooding\nin low lying areas along the river.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 2:30 PM MST Monday the stage was 2.7 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 7.0 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to rise 